# Security headers for GIMEK's Boutique.
#
# This file is read by Netlify and Cloudflare Pages as-is. Vercel,
# Apache and nginx want the same headers expressed their own way —
# README.md has the translations.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy here must stay in step with the <meta>
# copy in index.html. The meta tag is the fallback for hosts that
# cannot set headers; this file is what applies when the host can.
# Two differences, both deliberate:
#   - frame-ancestors is here only. Browsers ignore it in a meta tag.
#   - the header wins wherever both are delivered, because the two
#     policies are enforced together and this one is no looser.
#
# The sha256 in script-src covers the pre-paint theme script inlined
# in index.html. Editing that script invalidates the hash and stops
# it running. README.md has the command that recomputes it.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-hlyHGsFTw4Q2qpZdlSwoZg37M+yF2lwOLTkNZkvliKU='; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data:; frame-src https://www.google.com https://maps.google.com; connect-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  # HSTS is a promise you cannot easily take back: once a browser has
  # seen this, it refuses plain HTTP to the domain for two years.
  # Every host named in README.md serves HTTPS by default, so it is
  # safe there. Delete the next line if the domain still has to answer
  # on plain HTTP for anything. It is deliberately not `preload`.
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
